<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#earl-of-clanricarde">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Earl of Clanricarde</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1543">1543</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Earl of Clanricarde is a title in the Peerage of Ireland created in 1543 for Ulick na gCeann Burke, chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-burgh">Burkes</a> of south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a>, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s policy of surrender and regrant. The earls held lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loughrea">Loughrea</a> and Portumna, and the later holders were mostly loyal to the crown during the Tudor and Stuart wars in Ireland. The 5th Earl was made Marquess of Clanricarde in 1646.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/earl-of-clanricarde.jpg" alt="Earl of Clanricarde" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coronet_of_a_British_Earl.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
